{"name":"British Shorthair","hex":"#5f6672","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"British Shorthair","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A medium-sized shorthaired domestic cat of a breed originating in Great Britain."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/British_Shorthair"}],"entries":[{"title":"British Shorthair","blocks":[{"text":"The British Shorthair is the pedigree version of the landrace of British domestic cat, with a distinctively stocky body, thick coat, and broad face. The most familiar colour variant is the \"British Blue\", with a solid grey-blue coat, copper-coloured eyes, and a medium-sized tail. The breed has also been bred in a wide range of other colours and patterns, including tabby and colourpoint."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Mystica_from_British_Empire_Cattery.jpg/330px-Mystica_from_British_Empire_Cattery.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/British_Shorthair"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e2/Blue_Shorthair_cat_English_type.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e2/Blue_Shorthair_cat_English_type.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"An early example of the \"English type\" Blue Shorthair, from Frances Simpson's Book of the Cat, 1903","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABlue_Shorthair_cat_English_type.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Xenophon_Windsor_Magazine_vol_IX_%28cropped%29.png/500px-Xenophon_Windsor_Magazine_vol_IX_%28cropped%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Xenophon_Windsor_Magazine_vol_IX_%28cropped%29.png/500px-Xenophon_Windsor_M